  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "First to the puck – battle and shot",
  "description": "Two lines, one in each corner at one end, and a coach in front of the net. The coach plays a medium-paced pass straight out, which is the starting signal. The first two players race for the puck; whoever gets control tries to score on the goalie at the other end, and the other tries to win the puck back.\n\nAim for game tempo and a real battle, but within the rules for the age group so no one gets hurt. Skate back along the boards after the shot. Vary it by starting the players on their knees or lying on their stomachs. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "React to the pass – not to the coach's movement."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Protect the puck with your body once you have it."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "If you did not get the puck: never give up, backcheck."
    }
  ],
